# Run artifacts: raw evidence kept locally, reported via the context item. The analysis
# tables are the exception -- they are aggregates and they are what the write-up cites.
# `results/` on its own would stop git descending, so the negation needs the glob.
results/*
!results/analysis/

# Fetched label sets for scripts/grader_check.py
.cache/

# The generated attack strings. data/prefill_manifest.json carries the table's sha256,
# so a rebuild is still checked against what the study ran on; the strings themselves
# stay on the machine that produced them.
data/prefills.csv
